# CVE-2026-39324: Rack::Session::Cookie fell back to the unverified
# coder when decryption failed. In unpacked_cookie_data
# (lib/rack/session/cookie.rb), a cookie the configured encryptors
# could not decrypt left session_data nil, and the branch
#
#   elsif !session_data && coder
#     session_data = coder.decode(cookie_data)
#
# handed the raw cookie to the coder -- Base64::Marshal by default,
# whose decode runs ::Marshal.load(super(str)). A forged plain
# Base64::Marshal cookie thereforee deserialized unauthenticated in
# any deployment that had configured :secrets (untrusted
# deserialization, CWE-502). The fixed revision adds encryptors.empty? to the
# guard, so a deployment with encryptors rejects the cookie instead of
# falling back.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap plus a configuration-shaped guard.
#
# 1. The taint chain is intact except for one hop. request.cookies[key]
#    is labelled code.HttpInput (ruby.input) and ::Marshal.load is
#    labelled code.Deserialization (ruby.sinks), but coder.decode never
#    resolves: Ruby dispatch reaches resolveTargets with no receiver
#    type (nothing records the type of @coder = options[:coder] ||=
#    Base64::Marshal.new -- an op-assign hides the constructor call at
#    lowering.go:3065, and the attr_reader spelling `coder` is not
#    linked to the ivar), so the call falls to the
#    unique-method-name-across-program fallback (lowering.go:5112).
#    `decode` is defined in six classes in cookie.rb, the fallback
#    short-circuits ambiguous, and taint terminates at the call. The
#    first test below reports the identical chain with one `decode`
#    definition in the file -- proving the source, the sink, and the
#    super(s) argument hop all work -- while the second, differing only
#    in a second class defining decode, stays silent.
# 2. The guard the fixed revision adds is runtime configuration, not dataflow.
#    With the ambiguity removed (single decode definition), the
#    patched form `elsif !session_data && encryptors.empty? && coder`
#    still reports VYQL-DESER-001 -- measured on the third test's
#    single-decode twin. The path cookie -> coder.decode ->
#    Marshal.load exists in both revisions; only the encryptor
#    configuration decides it, which taint cannot see. The 1380
#    counterweight fails: the one call the fixed revision leaves inside the
#    guarded method is encryptors.empty?, this library's own reader,
#    and a core.SafeDeserialization binding keyed on it would be this
#    patch's own vocabulary rather than anything derivable from the
#    documentation. Same family as the configuration-side fixes at
#    1514/1535/1540/1556/1557/1593.
#
# On the real tree at f43638c^ the scan reports 10 findings, identical
# at the fixed revision; the Marshal.load rows source from library.param-source
# (the decode parameter itself), not the cookie. When Ruby receiver
# types land, tests two and three start reporting and must be
# re-measured against the real revisions.

test "rack session cookie fallback: a unique coder decode reports the unverified deserialization"
  lang ruby
  file lib/rack/session/cookie.rb
  expect VYQL-DESER-001
  code
  ```
  class Coder
    def decode(str)
      Marshal.load(super(str)) rescue nil
    end
  end

  class Session
    attr_reader :coder

    def initialize(options = {})
      @coder = options[:coder] ||= Coder.new
    end

    def unpacked_cookie_data(request)
      if cookie_data = request.cookies["rack.session"]
        session_data = coder.decode(cookie_data)
      end
      session_data || {}
    end
  end
  ```

test "rack session cookie fallback: a second decode definition silences the chain"
  lang ruby
  file lib/rack/session/cookie.rb
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  code
  ```
  class CoderBase
    def decode(str)
      Base64.decode64(str)
    end
  end

  class Coder < CoderBase
    def decode(str)
      Marshal.load(super(str)) rescue nil
    end
  end

  class Session
    attr_reader :coder

    def initialize(options = {})
      @coder = options[:coder] ||= Coder.new
    end

    def unpacked_cookie_data(request)
      if cookie_data = request.cookies["rack.session"]
        session_data = coder.decode(cookie_data)
      end
      session_data || {}
    end
  end
  ```

test "rack session cookie fallback: the encryptors.empty? guard does not clear the path"
  lang ruby
  file lib/rack/session/cookie.rb
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  code
  ```
  class CoderBase
    def decode(str)
      Base64.decode64(str)
    end
  end

  class Coder < CoderBase
    def decode(str)
      Marshal.load(super(str)) rescue nil
    end
  end

  class Encryptor
    def decrypt(data)
      raise "invalid message"
    end
  end

  class Session
    attr_reader :coder, :encryptors

    def initialize(options = {})
      @encryptors = [Encryptor.new]
      @coder = options[:coder] ||= Coder.new
    end

    def unpacked_cookie_data(request)
      if cookie_data = request.cookies["rack.session"]
        session_data = nil
        encryptors.each do |encryptor|
          begin
            session_data = encryptor.decrypt(cookie_data)
            break
          rescue
            next
          end
        end
        if !session_data && encryptors.empty? && coder
          session_data = coder.decode(cookie_data)
        end
      end
      session_data || {}
    end
  end
  ```
